    "title": "Here's How to Tell Google You Want More of Our Content - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Townsquare Media ,\n9 hours ago\nIt can be hard to find news and information from media sources you trust. That’s why Google has recently added a new feature: Preferred Sources .\nBy adding Talk 103.9 and 1340 as a “preferred source,” you signal to Google that you would like to see content from our site at the top of your news-related search results, when available. This gives you more personal control over the results you get – and lets you support your favorite news and information sources.\nWe’d love it if you added us as one of your trusted media sources on Google!\nHow to set us as a preferred source on Google It’s pretty easy to add a site as your preferred source.\nAdding Us Directly From Account Sources 1. Access your ‘Sources’ menu directly at https://www.google.com/preferences/source .\n2. Search for, and place a check mark next to, kkam.com. You can also set us as a preferred source by clicking here . That’s it – you’re done!\nAdding Us On The Google Search Page 1. Search for a topic that’s in the news on Google. Or simply search the news by clicking here .\n2. Next to the “Top stories” header, click the Cards Star icon.\nGoogle Chrome 3. Search for, and place a check mark next to, our site’s name.\nGoogle Chrome 4. That’s it! You can click “Reload Results” or click the upper right “X” to close out of the source window.\nThank you! We appreciate your support.\nSource: Here’s How to Tell Google You Want More of Our Content",
